Business Justification for Polyglot Persistence
While relational systems offer the ACID guarantees required for account ledgers, they face scaling and structural challenges when handling:
High-volume, semi-structured clickstream telemetry, security context, and API device fingerprint audits.
Microsecond-latency distributed session states, temporary authorization tokens, and API rate limiting.
Complex multi-hop fraud detection networks (identifying mule accounts and shared device rings).
ApexPay implements a Polyglot Persistence Model, combining the relational core with three purpose-built NoSQL architectures:
Code
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                               APEXPAY DATA STORAGE TIERS                               |
+--------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------------------+
| Engine Archetype         | Technology Target     | Primary Business Functionality      |
+--------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------------------+
| Relational (RDBMS)       | PostgreSQL / Aurora   | Core double-entry accounts ledger   |
| Document Store           | MongoDB Atlas         | Dynamic audit trails and telemetry  |
| Key-Value Store          | Redis Cluster         | Idempotency keys, user sessions     |
| Graph Database           | Neo4j Enterprise      | Fraud prevention, AML ring analysis |
+--------------------------+-----------------------+-------------------------------------+
