5.3 Key-Value Store Specification: Idempotency & Rate Limiting
The Key-Value store operates entirely in-memory to provide microsecond response times for high-frequency operational guards.
Key Naming Conventions and Expiration Lifecycle
Code
Key Pattern: idempotency:token:{idempotency_key_value}
Data Type:   String (JSON serialized)
TTL:         86,400 seconds (24 Hours)
Value:       {"status": "COMMITTED", "txn_id": "UUID-771", "http_code": 200, "response_hash": "sha256-..."}

Key Pattern: ratelimit:customer:{customer_id}:window:{minute_timestamp}
Data Type:   Atomic Integer Counter
TTL:         60 seconds
Value:       "14" (Number of requests executed within the active window)
Suitability: Using fast in-memory key-value lookups allows the system to enforce rate limits and verify idempotency tokens before reaching the core relational database, protecting the ledger from duplicate payments and denial-of-service traffic.
5.4 Graph Database Specification: Real-Time Anti-Money Laundering (AML)
Relational databases struggle to query deep, multi-hop connection paths (e.g., checking "Who sent money to an account that shares a device with a known bad actor?"). Graph databases excel at these relationship-focused queries.
Code
GRAPH NODE AND EDGE SPECIFICATION:

[Customer Node] ──(OWNED_BY)──> [Device Node]
      │                               ▲
      │ (OWNS)                        │ (ACCESSED_FROM)
      ▼                               │
[Account Node] ──(TRANSFERRED_TO)──> [Account Node]
Node Structure
(:Customer {customer_id, full_name, kyc_status, risk_rating})
(:Account {account_number, currency, current_balance})
(:Device {device_id_hash, device_type, operating_system})
(:IPAddress {ip_string, autonomous_system, is_vpn})
Edge (Relationship) Structure
[:OWNS {opened_date}] connects Customer to Account
[:TRANSFERRED_TO {amount, timestamp, currency, reference}] connects Account to Account
[:AUTHENTICATED_WITH {timestamp, session_id}] connects Customer to Device
Fraud Detection Scenario: Money Mule Ring Identification
Graph pattern matching traverses these connections to detect suspicious circles where funds move across accounts that share identical device fingerprints or physical IP addresses:
Traverse outgoing transactions from target Account across 3 hops.
Cross-reference device identifiers used to authenticate those receiving accounts.
If distinct customers access their accounts from the same physical hardware, flag the entire ring for manual compliance review.
